From 2159e88b10f1d4c77cfb67041382b623b4462205 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pdale-boop <237306950+pdale-boop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:23:14 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Aurora: steps for the game's depth of field, and where it
 starts

Wind Waker's depth of field (drawDepth) draws a half-size copy of the
whole EFB back over the distance. Copies are made at the render scale, so
at 2x and up its blur shrank to a fraction of the game's; and where it
starts is fixed by the game's focus.

- aurora_set_game_dof (DOL_AURORA_GAME_DOF): how soft the blur is.
  0 none (a full-size copy), 1 half the default's, 2 the default (as
  before), 3 between, 4 the game's own blur at 1x at any render scale,
  the copy blurred on the GPU (tex_copy_conv: a separable blur of the
  colour copy, its strength from the scale).
- aurora_set_game_dof_start (DOL_AURORA_GAME_DOF_START): how much
  farther out it starts, 0 to 100. The game starts it at the camera's
  focus or its room's PhotoDepth, as minus the depth's second byte m;
  there the depth is about 1 - near/distance, so moving the start k
  times as far out is m' = 256 - (256 - m) / k, with no near plane
  needed, and it still follows the camera. k doubles about every 29
  steps, to about 11 at 100 (farther showed no difference in a
  full-screen 1x picture). The draw is found by its blend stage (a
  second stage of ZERO, APREV, TEXA, A0, times 4, after a compare).

Both start at the game's behaviour (step 2, start 0), so nothing changes
unless a host sets them.
